                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "197da72e-9c5e-4b9e-adad-d030e6251a85",
                        "entry_id": "46ddb36c-685d-3e95-8b1d-4e9470ae1ef0",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural",
                            "masculine",
                            "feminine"
                        ],
                        "form": "inimitables"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "b3654422-9dd5-39aa-9775-72d2cb208b32",
                        "entry_id": "46ddb36c-685d-3e95-8b1d-4e9470ae1ef0",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Qui ne peut pas être imité."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "01a09815-413e-404d-8c79-cb241eb2787e",
                                "sense_id": "b3654422-9dd5-39aa-9775-72d2cb208b32",
                                "text": "Les femmes ont un inimitable talent pour exprimer leurs sentiments sans employer de trop vives paroles ; leur éloquence est surtout dans l'accent, dans le geste, l'attitude et les regards."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5316f1ee-f43d-433a-a61d-d2c3fa0628df",
                                "sense_id": "b3654422-9dd5-39aa-9775-72d2cb208b32",
                                "text": "Ce mouvement était inimitable; il avait la canaillerie, l'impudence, la persuasion d'un dresseur, d'un tombeur de femmes."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e651a2c1-fdd5-4118-80fc-290403c09221",
                                "sense_id": "b3654422-9dd5-39aa-9775-72d2cb208b32",
                                "text": "En 2007, il s'est installé dans les murs de l'une des plus illustres saurisseries de Boulogne-sur-Mer pour fumer ses harengs dans des coresses, ces fours à bois qui ressemblent à de hautes armoires et où le poisson prend cette saveur et cet aspect inimitables que procure le lent fumage à l'ancienne (vingt-quatre à quarante-huit heures)."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2cecb1c4-8758-4e6d-9b22-f84cef5c851e",
                                "sense_id": "b3654422-9dd5-39aa-9775-72d2cb208b32",
                                "text": "On tourna le dos à l'Hôtel des monnaies, la vainqueresse musardait, feignant de rien deviner de mes émois ni de la captivité dans laquelle, d'un inimitable balancement fessier, elle m'avait jeté."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "dcb4b72c-1da8-40e0-a899-c923f0d81550",
                        "source_entry_id": "46ddb36c-685d-3e95-8b1d-4e9470ae1ef0",
                        "source_sense_id": "b3654422-9dd5-39aa-9775-72d2cb208b32",
                        "target_lang_word": "inimitable",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "inimitable",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "94888005-eb27-305b-80bd-c8be73360d85",
                                        "entry_id": "3fc55e56-f377-3689-b3b6-d4fcb28104ed",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Beyond imitation, surpassing all others; matchless."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "03da3883-76ab-4a57-bb2c-05f03807378f",
                                                "sense_id": "94888005-eb27-305b-80bd-c8be73360d85",
                                                "text": "Moreover, a perfect Medal has its Profile and out-ſtroaks ſharp (Nummus aſper) and by no means rugged; the Figures clean and well poliſh'd; the Contours neatly trimm'd, and exactly round and carefully preſerv'd; that the Extancy and Relievos correſpond with the Ingraving, and have not ſuffer'd in Percuſſion; in all which, there is a certain Spirit of Antiquity and Excellency to be diſcern'd in Antient Medals almoſt inimitable."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c4511b52-9627-462f-ac9e-21c31efa2c70",
                                                "sense_id": "94888005-eb27-305b-80bd-c8be73360d85",
                                                "text": "Sterling himself, though he had the most picturesque and inimitable vocabulary of vituperation, was highly squeamish about ordinary smut or profanity. He had indeed that nice-Nelliness which is often characteristic of the Don Juan type."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d3a535c5-48c6-4032-902a-3a8344090f1b",
                                                "sense_id": "94888005-eb27-305b-80bd-c8be73360d85",
                                                "text": "Let's see you pay for your drink in your own inimitable fashion, huh? A song, Denton! How about it?"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "21bde835-188f-46db-b817-bc50f11d1e14",
                        "source_entry_id": "46ddb36c-685d-3e95-8b1d-4e9470ae1ef0",
